===Etymology===
Borrowed from a medieval Low German variant of [[Theodoric]], Germanic ''þeud'' "people" + ''ric'' "ruler", and revived in the nineteenth century. 

===Pronunciation===
*:Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-ɛrɪk|-ɛrɪk]]

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{given name|male}}, popular in the UK in mid-twentieth century.


